            "date_published": "2025-09-23T01:25:20.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417399601\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41134\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41134/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41134\">#41134</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41252",
            "title": "Reference for stage 3 upsert",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-23T06:14:26.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-22T22:30:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are still <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39393#issuecomment-2851420219\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39393/hovercard\">several Learn articles</a> not linked from the learnsidebar. The ones we want to keep should really be linked in some way. This PR adds an \"Additional tutorials\" subsection at the end of the extension modules to contain the additional tutorials.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In one case (performance), I didn't add it into \"Additional tutorials\"; I just moved the article so that the slug made more sense, and then added it into the main flow of that module.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In one case (forms), I edited an article to make it a) more useful and b) actually make sense in the context of earlier forms articles in the same module (we don't want to cover all those CSS techniques only to then say \"don't style form elements\" in a later article).</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41242",
            "title": "Add extensions additional tutorials links to learnsidebar",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-23T15:01:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-22T11:21:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 aligns with Chrome and Safari such that a cross origin iframe now requires sticky activation in order to redirect the top level page via <code class=\"notranslate\">window.top.location</code> (in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501</a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a release note and also a section in the iframe docs explaining the expected behavior as it is now.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417409664\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41138/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138\">#41138</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41237",
            "title": "FF144 Relnote+Doc: Cross origin iframe requires user interaction for top navigation",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-23T18:56:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-22T04:20:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #23847.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1553771549\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23847\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/23847/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23847\">#23847</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #36764.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2653767824\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/36764\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/36764/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/36764\">#36764</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3437880034\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41232\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41232/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41232\">#41232</a>, I added a discussion about canvas grid-pixel alignment. This enables me to refer to that section elsewhere when we discuss sharp shape edges.</p>",
